&lt;p&gt;I get this question a lot, so I’ll answer it from what I actually did.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the recruitment ATS/CRM I worked on, the frontend was first built in WeWeb. Later we rebuilt the whole frontend in React 19 + TypeScript, and most of that work was done with Claude Code. So I’ve used both on the same product, with real users.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My answer is simple: if you’ve never coded before, start with WeWeb. If you already have some notions of code, start with React.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why WeWeb if you’ve never coded
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;WeWeb is easy to pick up. You put elements on a page, connect them to your data, and add workflows that run when someone clicks a button or submits a form.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What I like is that it teaches you how a frontend works while you build:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you pick up in WeWeb:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;how a page fetches data from an API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;where that data is kept while the page is open&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;workflows: when this happens, do this, then that&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;variables and conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;what to do when a request fails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You do the same things in React later. In WeWeb you just do them visually first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It’s also a good option if you don’t want to vibe-code everything with AI. You build each part yourself, so you understand what you made. (I wrote more about that in &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/blog/low-code-vs-vibe-coding/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;low-code or vibe coding&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why React is easier to get into now
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few years ago React was harder to start with. You had to set up the project, learn the tooling and write everything by hand before anything worked.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With Claude Code that’s different. You describe the page, it writes the components, and you review and fix what it wrote. You can build a lot more in a lot less time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That’s how we did our migration. We added React pages one by one while the WeWeb app was still running, until React was the whole frontend. We used TanStack Query, React Hook Form, Zod and React Router.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WeWeb app in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React pages added one by one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both running during the migration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React becomes the whole frontend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;How we moved from WeWeb to React&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a big app that keeps growing, I’d pick React today because you have full control over the code. (More on my &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/react-developer/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React work&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  React is harder to debug
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In WeWeb, when something breaks, you open the workflow and check each step. You can see what the API returned and which variable is empty.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In React the problem can be in a component, a hook, the state, the cache, a request or a type. You check the console and the network tab, and follow the data through several files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If AI wrote a big part of the code, a beginner will have a hard time here, because you’re debugging code you didn’t write and don’t fully understand yet. That’s where I see most people get stuck.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WeWeb&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you see each workflow step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you see what the API returned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fewer places for a bug to hide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;less freedom when the app gets big&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;full control over the code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI writes it much faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;bugs can be spread across files&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you need to read code to fix it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Which one to start with
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start with WeWeb if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you’ve never written code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you want to see how data and workflows work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you want to build something real soon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you don’t want AI doing everything for you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start with React if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you already know some code, even a little&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you studied programming or tried it before&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you want to learn the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you plan to build bigger apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Starting with WeWeb doesn’t lock you in. When you move to React later, you’ll already know how data is fetched, what state is and how a workflow runs, so it’s mostly about learning to write it as code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you already know some code, I wouldn’t spend months in a visual tool. Go to React, use AI to go faster, and read what it writes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a large frontend I’d use React today. But WeWeb got us far quickly, and I’d still recommend it to someone who has never coded. (For the bigger picture, see &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/blog/low-code-vs-full-code/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;low-code vs full-code&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;I first posted this &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/blog/weweb-vs-react/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;on my blog&lt;/a&gt;, where it’s also in French and Arabic. What did you start with, and would you pick the same again?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the member list in almost any app. Most people never upload a photo, so you see a column of identical grey silhouettes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8h75fdqsh8y9mo4sgtfq.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8h75fdqsh8y9mo4sgtfq.png" alt="when not to use it" width="800" height="377"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The usual fixes each come with a catch:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Initials&lt;/strong&gt; work until two people are both "JS". And white letters on bright tiles often fail contrast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Random colors&lt;/strong&gt; change on every render, unless you add a database column to store them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Generated avatars&lt;/strong&gt; are the right idea, but many use &lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt; or hard-coded SVG IDs. Then the server draws one face, the browser draws another, and your console fills with hydration warnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted avatars I would never have to think about again. Same input, same bytes, on every server, in every browser and in every release. That became &lt;a href="https://github.com/Inlaylab/Opaline" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Opaline&lt;/a&gt;. This post covers what it gives you, how to use it, and the engineering that makes the promise hold.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why you might want it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;You want&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What Opaline does&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Users you can tell apart&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Each seed gets its own face, colors and shape. Five styles.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Avatars that never change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Same seed and options give a byte-identical SVG for all of 1.x, checked in CI&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No hydration warnings&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Server and client produce the same markup. Tested in Next, Nuxt, SvelteKit and Angular SSR.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One library across your stack&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One core and components for React 18+, Vue 3.5+, Svelte 5.20+, Angular 20–22, plus a Web Component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A small bundle&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Core is &lt;strong&gt;1.27 kB&lt;/strong&gt; gzipped with zero dependencies. With the largest style it's 5.57 kB.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Photos when users have them&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pass &lt;code&gt;src&lt;/code&gt;. If it's missing or broken, the generated face stays.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Brand colors and dark mode&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Colors are CSS variables, so you restyle without regenerating&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Accessible initials&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Letters clear WCAG AA (4.5:1) on every palette, checked for 2,100 seed/palette pairs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No license review&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;MIT for the code &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; the art&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Using it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install the package for your framework. Each one pulls in the core.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm i @inlaylab/opaline-react   &lt;span class="c"&gt;# or -vue, -svelte, -angular, -element&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt; (server-component safe, React 18 or later):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AvatarGroup&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline-react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline/clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;look&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;photo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AvatarGroup&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;look&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;members&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Project members&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vue 3.5+ / Nuxt:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight vue"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:seed=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"user.email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:look=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"clay"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"user.photo"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"user.name"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Svelte 5.20+ / SvelteKit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight svelte"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;seed=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;look=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;photo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Angular 20–22&lt;/strong&gt; (standalone, OnPush, works zoneless):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;op-avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;[seed]=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;[look]=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"clay"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;[src]=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"photo"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No framework:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;type=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"module"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline-element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;opaline-avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;seed=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"ada@inlay.dev"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;look=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"clay"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;finish=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"gloss"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;size=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"64"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/opaline-avatar&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No DOM at all.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;createAvatar&lt;/code&gt; returns a plain string, so it works in an API route, a build script or an email template:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline/clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;ada@inlay.dev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hood&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ears&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bunny&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flk8bcu9lnrdlwy57g8lq.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flk8bcu9lnrdlwy57g8lq.png" alt="createAvatar code next to the avatar it generates" width="800" height="400"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any option you set pins that part of the avatar. The seed fills in the rest.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Need a PNG for an OG card, a push notification or a profile-photo upload? &lt;code&gt;toPng&lt;/code&gt; (688 B) does it in the browser with no dependencies:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toPng&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline/png&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;blob&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;toPng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;512&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now the interesting part: how "same bytes everywhere" actually holds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. The seed is the only input, so normalize it first
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users type &lt;code&gt;Ada@Inlay.dev&lt;/code&gt; with a trailing space on one form and &lt;code&gt;ada@inlay.dev&lt;/code&gt; on another. If those give different faces, you get a bug report. So every seed goes through this first:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;EMAIL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;[^\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;[^\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+$/&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;normalizeSeed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;''&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;normalize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;NFC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;EMAIL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLowerCase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;NFC matters more than it looks. &lt;code&gt;Zoë&lt;/code&gt; can arrive as one code point (&lt;code&gt;ë&lt;/code&gt;) or two (&lt;code&gt;e&lt;/code&gt; plus a combining diaeresis), depending on the OS and keyboard. Without NFC those are two different people.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only emails are lower-cased. Usernames like &lt;code&gt;Ada&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ada&lt;/code&gt; can be different accounts, so they keep their case.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. No Math.random(): a seeded PRNG with forks
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The seed goes through &lt;strong&gt;xmur3&lt;/strong&gt;, a small string hash, which seeds &lt;strong&gt;sfc32&lt;/strong&gt;, a fast 32-bit PRNG. Both fit in a few lines and give identical results on every JavaScript engine, because they use only &lt;code&gt;Math.imul&lt;/code&gt;, shifts and &lt;code&gt;| 0&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createRng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Rng&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;xmur3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sfc32&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Early sfc32 outputs are weakly mixed; skip them.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;++&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;float&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// A fork depends only on the seed and label, never on earlier draws.&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;fork&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createRng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;u0000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;fork&lt;/code&gt; line is the most important decision in the library.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A naive generator draws everything from one stream: shape, then color, then eyes, then mouth. Now add a new eyebrow option in a later release. It takes one draw from the stream, and every draw after it shifts. &lt;strong&gt;Every existing user's mouth changes.&lt;/strong&gt; That's a breaking change you didn't mean to ship.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With forks, each feature gets its own stream, keyed by the seed and a label:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fork&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;pick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;float&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;fork('color')&lt;/code&gt; gives the same numbers whether it's called first or last, or after ten new features. New features get new labels. Old faces never move.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;\u0000&lt;/code&gt; separator stops a seed of &lt;code&gt;"ab"&lt;/code&gt; with label &lt;code&gt;"c"&lt;/code&gt; from colliding with seed &lt;code&gt;"a"&lt;/code&gt; and label &lt;code&gt;"bc"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. SVG IDs that are unique per page and identical across hydration
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SVG gradients and filters need &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;s. That creates two separate bugs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Two avatars on one page share &lt;code&gt;id="grad"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; The second one silently uses the first one's gradient, so the wrong colors appear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The server and the client invent different IDs.&lt;/strong&gt; You get a hydration mismatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Opaline builds every ID from two parts:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createIds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;u0000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;u0000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;stableStringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;instance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// id('grad') -&amp;gt; "a&amp;lt;7-char hash&amp;gt;-grad-&amp;lt;instance&amp;gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The prefix&lt;/strong&gt; is a hash of the seed, the style and the options. The same seed with different options never shares &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;defs&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;stableStringify&lt;/code&gt; sorts the keys, so option order never matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The instance suffix&lt;/strong&gt; comes from each framework's SSR-safe ID primitive:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Package&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Instance from&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Minimum version&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;useId()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React 18, the version that introduced &lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vue&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;useId()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vue 3.5. Multiple apps on a page set &lt;code&gt;app.config.idPrefix&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Svelte&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;$props.id()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Svelte 5.20&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Angular&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;An injectable per-app counter. Server and client render in the same order, so the numbers match.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Angular 20&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Web Component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A module counter. There is no SSR, so only uniqueness matters.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Any modern browser&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That table is also why the minimum versions are what they are. &lt;strong&gt;1.1.2&lt;/strong&gt; lowered React to 18 for exactly this reason: &lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt; exists there, so nothing else was blocking it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. Defaults are invisible
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One rule turned out to matter a lot: &lt;strong&gt;an option set to its default must give byte-for-byte the same output as leaving it unset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without that rule, &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar finish="soft"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; hash to different ID prefixes, so a refactor that spells out a default changes your markup. Each style declares its defaults, and &lt;code&gt;createAvatar&lt;/code&gt; drops matching values before hashing:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;stableStringify&lt;/code&gt; also skips &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; values. Wrappers pass every prop through, and &lt;code&gt;{ shape: undefined }&lt;/code&gt; must not hash differently from &lt;code&gt;{}&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Proof, not promises
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"Deterministic" is an easy word to write in a README. Here is how the repo checks it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  A frozen checksum file: 4,000 hashes
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0e14zxgfssidzpuqfg8y.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0e14zxgfssidzpuqfg8y.png" alt="SSR" width="800" height="326"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;frozen-1.json&lt;/code&gt; holds 4,000 SHA-256 digests (first 16 hex characters):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;100 seeds&lt;/strong&gt; shaped like real input: emails, &lt;code&gt;Person B12&lt;/code&gt;-style names, base36 IDs, plain numbers, and Unicode with emoji (&lt;code&gt;Zoë Nguyễn 4 😀&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;40 option sets&lt;/strong&gt; across all five styles: every finish, every shape, palettes, hood and ears, custom initials text.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`1.x output is frozen: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;FROZEN_SEEDS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;opts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;changed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;FROZEN_SEEDS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;manifest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]?.[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;changed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Output changed for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;...`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toEqual&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If one byte of one avatar changes, CI fails and names the seed. A second test checks that the manifest still covers every case, so nobody can make the guarantee pass by deleting rows. The only way to change the output is to regenerate the file on purpose, and that means a major version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's what lets you cache an avatar on a CDN forever, store the SVG in a database, or put it in an email that will be opened in three years.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Real SSR apps, hydrated in a real browser
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Four sample apps live in the repo: &lt;strong&gt;Next (App Router, RSC), Nuxt, SvelteKit and Angular SSR (zoneless)&lt;/strong&gt;. For each one, Playwright:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;starts the production server and fetches the HTML;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;asserts that every &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; in the page is unique, and that the named avatar has &lt;code&gt;role="img"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;aria-label&lt;/code&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;loads the page in Chromium and fails on any console message matching &lt;code&gt;/hydrat/i&lt;/code&gt;, any error and any page exception;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;compares the hydrated DOM with the server HTML&lt;/strong&gt;: every avatar's root attributes and its &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;svg&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; must be exactly what the server sent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 4 exists because of something I found while writing step 3. &lt;strong&gt;Production Svelte repairs a hydration mismatch silently.&lt;/strong&gt; No warning, no error. The page looks fine, the console is clean, and the bug is invisible. Watching the console isn't enough. You have to diff the DOM.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Size, enforced
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;size-limit&lt;/code&gt; runs in CI with a budget for every entry point. These are today's numbers, minified and gzipped:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Import&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Size&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Budget&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;createAvatar&lt;/code&gt; (core)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1.27 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Aura&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2.52 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Initials&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2.86 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Morph&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4.90 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Gradient&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5.13 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5.25 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Clay&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5.57 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;8 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React wrapper (avatar + group)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;854 B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1.5 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;PNG export&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;688 B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Styles are separate imports, so you only ship the ones you use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Speed
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A perf test builds 500 Clay avatars with the gloss finish, the heaviest combination. It warms the JIT, then keeps the best of five runs. On my laptop (Node 24) that's &lt;strong&gt;56–63 ms, about 120 µs per avatar&lt;/strong&gt;. CI fails above 250 ms, so a slow shared runner doesn't flake the build. A member list of 200 people costs you around 25 ms of CPU, once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What broke along the way
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I broke my own promise once, on purpose.&lt;/strong&gt; 1.1.0 shipped Initials with white letters. On the brightest tiles that was as low as &lt;strong&gt;1.9:1&lt;/strong&gt; contrast, far below the 4.5:1 that WCAG AA asks for. Shipping unreadable letters for the rest of 1.x seemed worse than changing them. So 1.1.1 changed exactly one thing: the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;text&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; fill on non-pastel palettes is now a deep shade of the tile's own hue. Nothing else changed: no shapes, no other styles. A new test checks 300 seeds on each of the 7 palettes and fails if any pair falls below 4.5:1. The README lists this as the one deliberate exception.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt; output isn't a valid SVG ID fragment.&lt;/strong&gt; Depending on the version, React's IDs contain characters such as &lt;code&gt;:&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;:r1:&lt;/code&gt; in React 18) or &lt;code&gt;«»&lt;/code&gt;. Those characters cause trouble inside &lt;code&gt;url(#…)&lt;/code&gt; references, so the wrapper strips everything except word characters and dashes before it uses the suffix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; changed the hash.&lt;/strong&gt; Wrappers forward every prop, so the core saw &lt;code&gt;{ shape: undefined }&lt;/code&gt; and hashed it differently from &lt;code&gt;{}&lt;/code&gt;. The result was a different ID prefix for the same avatar, depending on which wrapper rendered it. That's why &lt;code&gt;stableStringify&lt;/code&gt; now filters &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A silent Svelte fix hid a real mismatch&lt;/strong&gt;, as described above. That's why the e2e diffs the DOM and doesn't trust the console.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  When not to use it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want dozens of art styles, or an image URL from a hosted HTTP API with no code at all: use &lt;a href="https://www.dicebear.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;DiceBear&lt;/a&gt;. It's excellent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You're React-only and want minimal abstract shapes in your exact brand palette: &lt;a href="https://boringavatars.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Boring Avatars&lt;/a&gt; is lovely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need server-side PNG with zero setup: Opaline's &lt;code&gt;forRaster()&lt;/code&gt; prepares the SVG, but you still bring a rasterizer such as &lt;code&gt;@resvg/resvg-js&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://inlaylab.github.io/Opaline/compare/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;comparison page&lt;/a&gt; goes row by row, including the rows where the others win.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🎨 &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://inlaylab.github.io/Opaline/playground/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Playground&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: type your own name. Every setting lives in the URL, so you can share an exact avatar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⭐ &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/Inlaylab/Opaline" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: MIT for code and art.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;code&gt;npm i @inlaylab/opaline&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One question I'd really like your take on: &lt;strong&gt;is "byte-identical within a major version" the right contract?&lt;/strong&gt; Or would you rather have "looks the same" and let me fix rendering details in minor releases? I went with bytes because it makes CDN caching and email trivially safe, but it does make every bug fix a judgement call.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your site has a dark mode. Then a client asks, "Can we also have a blue theme? And a green one? Oh, and red!" 😅&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suddenly you are staring at &lt;code&gt;dark:bg-gray-900 blue:bg-blue-900 green:bg-green-900 red:bg-red-900&lt;/code&gt; on every element. That is a lot of repeated classes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is a cleaner way. You define every theme's colors &lt;strong&gt;once&lt;/strong&gt; in your global CSS. To switch themes, you change &lt;strong&gt;one class&lt;/strong&gt; on the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; element. No page refresh, no HTML changes, no per-element theme classes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ready to see how it works? 🚀&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What Is a Multi-Theme System in Next.js?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A multi-theme system lets users switch between more than two color schemes, such as light, dark, blue, green, and red. The switch happens instantly, with no reload.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of a &lt;strong&gt;TV remote&lt;/strong&gt;. The TV (your HTML) stays exactly the same. You press a button (change one class) and the colors change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The idea has three parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CSS variables&lt;/strong&gt; hold the colors, like &lt;code&gt;--background&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--primary&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, like &lt;code&gt;blue&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;red&lt;/code&gt;, decides which set of values is active.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Your components&lt;/strong&gt; use names like &lt;code&gt;bg-background&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;text-foreground&lt;/code&gt;, never specific colors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your components never know which theme is active. They just ask for "the background color" and the CSS answers.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Why This Topic Matters
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Theming gets messy fast when colors are written directly into components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adding a new theme means editing many files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rebranding means hunting through the whole codebase for color classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Markup gets longer and harder to read.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With the variable approach, a new theme is one new block in one CSS file. Components stay untouched.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Benefits with Real-Life Examples
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clean HTML and JSX.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;className="bg-background text-foreground"&lt;/code&gt; replaces a long chain of per-theme classes. A card component looks the same in every theme.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One place for all colors.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Your client says, "Make the green theme a bit softer." You change one value in &lt;code&gt;globals.css&lt;/code&gt;, and every button, card, and navbar follows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Easy to add new themes.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Want a purple theme? Add a &lt;code&gt;.purple { ... }&lt;/code&gt; block. No component changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instant switching, no refresh.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Changing a class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; makes the browser re-apply styles. There is no page reload, and React does not need to re-render your components just to change colors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Less repeated code.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
You are not generating and shipping theme-specific variants for every element, which keeps your markup and CSS leaner. (It will not magically shrink your app by half, but the duplication really does go away.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step-by-Step: Build It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This guide assumes the &lt;strong&gt;Next.js App Router&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Tailwind CSS v4&lt;/strong&gt;. A note for Tailwind v3 users appears later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Step 1: Define Your Themes in &lt;code&gt;globals.css&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;"tailwindcss"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;/* Default (light) theme */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nd"&gt;:root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#111827&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#f3f4f6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#4f46e5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;color-scheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.dark&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#0b0f19&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#e5e7eb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#151b2b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#818cf8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#0b0f19&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;color-scheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.blue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#eff6ff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#1e3a8a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#dbeafe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#2563eb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.green&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#f0fdf4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#14532d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#dcfce7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#16a34a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.red&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#fef2f2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#7f1d1d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#fee2e2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#dc2626&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every theme defines the &lt;strong&gt;same variable names&lt;/strong&gt; with different values. That is the whole trick. 💡&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Step 2: Connect the Variables to Tailwind
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;inline&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now &lt;code&gt;bg-background&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;text-foreground&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;bg-card&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;bg-primary&lt;/code&gt; work as normal Tailwind classes. They read the live CSS variable, so they follow whichever theme class is active.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Step 3: Use Semantic Classes in Your Components
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PricingCard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"rounded-xl bg-card p-6 text-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text-xl font-bold"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Pro Plan&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Everything you need to ship faster.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mt-4 rounded-lg bg-primary px-4 py-2 text-primary-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        Get Started
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;There are no &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;blue:&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;red:&lt;/code&gt; classes anywhere. This markup works for every theme you will ever add.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Step 4: Create the Theme Switcher
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// components/theme-switcher.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;blue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;green&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;red&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ThemeSwitcher&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;applyTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;documentElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;remove&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex gap-2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;applyTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"rounded-md bg-primary px-3 py-1 text-sm capitalize text-primary-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Clicking a button removes the old theme class and adds the new one. The colors change instantly. The choice is saved in &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; so it survives a reload.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Step 5: Avoid the "Flash of Wrong Theme"
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You have probably seen this: the page loads white, then flips to dark a moment later. It happens because the saved theme is applied only after React loads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is a tiny inline script that runs &lt;strong&gt;before the page paints&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/layout.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;RootLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="na"&gt;__html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`
              try {
                var t = localStorage.getItem('theme');
                if (t) document.documentElement.classList.add(t);
              } catch (e) {}
            `&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"bg-background text-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; is needed because the script changes the &lt;code&gt;class&lt;/code&gt; before React hydrates. Without it, React may warn about a mismatch.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Comparison: Per-Element Theme Classes vs CSS Variables
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Per-element classes (&lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;red:&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;CSS variables + one class&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Markup length&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Grows with every theme&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stays the same&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Adding a new theme&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Edit many components&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Add one CSS block&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Changing a color&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Search across files&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Edit one value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Best for&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Quick one-off tweaks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Real multi-theme apps&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Per-element classes are not "wrong". For a simple light/dark site they work fine. But once you go beyond two themes, variables win on maintainability.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Best Tips and Do's &amp;amp; Don'ts
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do ✅&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;strong&gt;semantic names&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;background&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;primary&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;card&lt;/code&gt;) instead of color names (&lt;code&gt;blue-500&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define &lt;strong&gt;the same set of variables in every theme&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set &lt;code&gt;color-scheme&lt;/code&gt; for dark themes so native elements like scrollbars and form inputs match.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test text contrast in every theme. A readable blue theme can still hide text in the red one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Don't ❌&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't put theme-specific colors directly in components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't forget the pre-paint script, or users will see a flash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't skip &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; if you use that script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tailwind v3 note:&lt;/strong&gt; v3 has no &lt;code&gt;@theme&lt;/code&gt; block. Map the variables in &lt;code&gt;tailwind.config.js&lt;/code&gt; instead, for example &lt;code&gt;background: "var(--background)"&lt;/code&gt;. If you want opacity modifiers like &lt;code&gt;bg-primary/50&lt;/code&gt; in v3, store the variables as RGB channels (like &lt;code&gt;253 110 78&lt;/code&gt;) and use &lt;code&gt;rgb(var(--primary) / &amp;lt;alpha-value&amp;gt;)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefer a library?&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/pacocoursey/next-themes" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;next-themes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; supports custom theme names through its &lt;code&gt;themes&lt;/code&gt; prop and handles storage and the flash problem for you. The CSS-variable idea in this article works the same way with it.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Common Mistakes People Make
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt; plus custom variants for every theme.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
It feels natural because that is how dark mode is usually taught. The fix is to define semantic variables once.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forgetting to remove the old class.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
If you only add &lt;code&gt;red&lt;/code&gt; and never remove &lt;code&gt;blue&lt;/code&gt;, both classes stay on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, and CSS order decides who wins. Always remove the old theme class first.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missing variables in one theme.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
If &lt;code&gt;.green&lt;/code&gt; forgets &lt;code&gt;--card&lt;/code&gt;, it inherits the value from &lt;code&gt;:root&lt;/code&gt;, so you get odd colors. Keep every theme's variable list identical.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reading &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; during server rendering.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; only exists in the browser. Use it inside event handlers, effects, or the inline script, not in server components.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ignoring accessibility.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
A pretty theme with low contrast is a bad theme. Check readability for every one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the recipe again:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define each theme's colors &lt;strong&gt;once&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;code&gt;globals.css&lt;/code&gt; using CSS variables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map those variables to semantic Tailwind colors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use classes like &lt;code&gt;bg-background&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;text-primary&lt;/code&gt; in your components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switch themes by changing &lt;strong&gt;one class&lt;/strong&gt; on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add a tiny pre-paint script so users never see a flash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The result is cleaner JSX, a single place to manage colors, and instant theme switching with no refresh. Adding a new theme becomes a ten-line job. 😊&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If this helped, you can read more practical dev guides at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://hamidrazadev.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;hamidrazadev.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. Share it with a developer friend who is still typing &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt; on every div 😄, and tell me in the comments which theme you would add first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI chat apps look simple: a prompt box, a streaming response, maybe citations. Under the hood, session management gets messy fast. How do you persist history across refreshes? How much context do you send to the model? What happens when the network hiccups or the user switches devices?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What "session" actually means
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A session isn't just a request/response pair. It covers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversation history: user and assistant messages across turns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Context window: the subset of history you actually send to the model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metadata: user ID, model version, feature flags, experiments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistence: how long sessions live, how they resume, where they're stored&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your UI needs to render history efficiently, stream new messages, handle reconnects and errors, and stay keyboard- and screen-reader-friendly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Core UI pattern: a session chat hook
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Centralizing message state, loading, errors, and basic persistence in a hook keeps components clean. Here's a simplified usage pattern:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useSessionChat&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/app/recipes/session/chat/hooks/use-session-chat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PromptInput&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/ui/composites/prompt-input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ResponseViewer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/ui/composites/response-viewer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SessionChatPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sendMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryLastMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSessionChat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;customer-support-session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex flex-col h-screen"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex-1 overflow-auto p-6 space-y-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text-right&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text-left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;assistant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponseViewer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"inline-block bg-primary-50 rounded-lg px-4 py-2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mt-4 p-3 rounded-md bg-red-50 text-sm text-red-800 flex items-center justify-between"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryLastMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
              &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"ml-4 text-xs underline"&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
              Retry
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"border-t p-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PromptInput&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;onSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;disabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;actionButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"send"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The heavy lifting: state management, pending states, basic retries: lives in the hook, not scattered across components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Where to store session data
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session data can live in three places, each with trade-offs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;In-memory (React state):&lt;/strong&gt; fast, lost on refresh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Local storage:&lt;/strong&gt; persists across reloads, single device only&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Backend storage:&lt;/strong&gt; durable and multi-device, requires APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hook stays agnostic about storage. Hydrating from local storage looks like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sendMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hydrateFromHistory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSessionChat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`chat:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;hydrateFromHistory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hydrateFromHistory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`chat:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now sessions survive a refresh without any UI changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Managing context windows
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LLM context windows force you to decide how much history to send each turn. Common strategies:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Last N turns:&lt;/strong&gt; send only the most recent messages (fast, simple)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Summarized history:&lt;/strong&gt; compress older messages into a running summary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Segmented sessions:&lt;/strong&gt; split long conversations into chapters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The UI should show the full history even if the model only sees part of it. A last-N strategy in your &lt;code&gt;sendMessage&lt;/code&gt; handler:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;buildModelPayload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ChatMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MAX_TURNS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;visibleHistory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;MAX_TURNS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;visibleHistory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The UI stays unchanged; only the payload builder shifts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Handling errors and retries gracefully
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Network hiccups and model errors are inevitable. Bad UIs lose the user's message, show generic banners, and offer no retry path. Better pattern:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preserve the user's message in history&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show per-message error states&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allow "Retry" on that specific message
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// inside message rendering&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;assistant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;retryMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mt-2 text-xs text-red-700 underline"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    Retry this response
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  Accessibility in session UIs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session management isn't just data: it's how the experience feels. Screen readers should announce new messages progressively. Keyboard users need to jump to the latest message, re-open prompts, and interact with citations and feedback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Streaming components need proper &lt;code&gt;aria-live&lt;/code&gt; regions, focusable elements for citations and controls, and predictable tab order across messages and input.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponseViewer&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;streamedContent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"markdown"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;showCitations&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"polite"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-atomic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;You don't have to become an ARIA expert to get a reasonable default.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Multi-session interfaces
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Many apps need multiple concurrent sessions: conversations per project, customer, or case. Pattern:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Left sidebar lists sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Right panel shows active session chat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both wired to the same session hook with different &lt;code&gt;sessionId&lt;/code&gt;s
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SessionsLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useUserSessions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// your data source&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex h-screen"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;aside&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"w-72 border-r bg-secondary-50"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* session list */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"w-full text-left px-4 py-2 hover:bg-secondary-100"&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;router&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/sessions/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text-sm font-medium"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text-xs text-secondary-600"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
              Updated &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;updatedAtRelative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;aside&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex-1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SessionChatPage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;key={sessionId}&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;SessionChatPage&lt;/code&gt; forces a clean remount when switching sessions, avoiding stale state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Session management checklist
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before shipping, verify:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;History&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users see past messages after refresh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Old messages don't break layout on mobile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long histories still feel fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear strategy for what goes to the model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not spamming the entire history on every call&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network errors preserve the user's message&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users can retry specific messages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timeouts and exceptions show clear, actionable errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New messages announced to screen readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keyboard users navigate messages and actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus doesn't jump unexpectedly during streaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-session&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sessions have stable IDs and URLs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switching sessions is fast and predictable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Session titles or metadata make sense to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The last item is a common gotcha: if you derive session titles from the first user message, make sure that title updates when the message edits or deletes, or you'll show stale labels in the sidebar.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a shorter version of a guide I wrote at Frontkit Studio. The &lt;a href="https://thefrontkit.com/blogs/session-management-in-ai-chat-applications?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=syndication" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;full post&lt;/a&gt; has the complete walkthrough.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbgx7pe2loku8clvbie4n.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbgx7pe2loku8clvbie4n.jpg" alt=" " width="800" height="450"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ftj6w92nqsdtjnrkfizqy.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ftj6w92nqsdtjnrkfizqy.jpg" alt=" " width="800" height="450"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fc3g3so1iejwaq8v5dng2.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fc3g3so1iejwaq8v5dng2.png" alt=" " width="800" height="329"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
A support agent can sound attentive while making a customer repeat the same troubleshooting step for the third time. I wanted the system to remember the outcome, not just the conversation—and to make that memory useful on the next ticket.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ResolveIQ is a support workflow built around that distinction. It combines ordinary operational records in PostgreSQL, a language model for drafting replies, and Hindsight for customer-level memory across conversations. The through-line is simple: a proposed fix is not a resolution. We need to know what was tried, whether it worked, and what the next response should avoid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  The system around the conversation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The application has a React and TypeScript frontend, a FastAPI backend, and PostgreSQL records for customers, tickets, conversations, messages, resolution attempts, and escalations. The support agent uses a server-side Groq client to generate a response. Hindsight provides retain, recall, and reflect operations for customer memories.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I keep those responsibilities separate. PostgreSQL owns facts that need explicit structure and predictable updates: the ticket state, the assignment, the message history, and each attempted solution’s outcome. Hindsight owns the customer memory that should inform a future interaction without turning every memory into a hand-maintained relational schema.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each customer gets a distinct Hindsight bank. The service derives its ID from a configured prefix and customer ID:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_bank_prefix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;-customer-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That boundary matters. A memory about one customer’s billing history should not be available while answering another customer’s ticket. It also gives the application a clear ownership rule: the ticket database is the system of record for workflow; Hindsight is the system used to retain and retrieve useful customer context.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The design uses &lt;a href="https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hindsight, an open-source agent memory system&lt;/a&gt;, through its Python client. Its &lt;a href="https://hindsight.vectorize.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;retain, recall, and reflect documentation&lt;/a&gt; maps cleanly to the lifecycle here: retain an interaction, recall relevant context before drafting, and reflect when a support agent wants a synthesized view of the customer’s history. That is one practical version of &lt;a href="https://vectorize.io/what-is-agent-memory" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;agent memory for applications&lt;/a&gt;: persistence that participates in the next decision, rather than a transcript archive nobody consults.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The important unit is an attempt
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The central design decision was to represent a proposed solution as a resolution attempt with an outcome. The model’s answer alone is not enough. The system records a proposed fix as &lt;code&gt;pending&lt;/code&gt;; a later response can mark that pending attempt &lt;code&gt;failed&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;succeeded&lt;/code&gt;. Human agents can also add and update attempts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That gives the next generation call two useful sources of context. The recent conversation explains what the customer said. The structured attempt list explains what the support process has already tried and whether it worked. Customer memory adds context that may span tickets: for example, recurring account conditions or an earlier resolution worth reusing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The prompt builder puts those sources into distinct sections instead of flattening everything into a vague summary:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;SYSTEM_INSTRUCTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;--- CURRENT CONTEXT ---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_info&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Customer Memories:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;memories_str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Prior Attempted Solutions on this Ticket (DO NOT REPEAT FAILED ONES):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;attempts_str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is intentionally explicit. A failed password reset and a customer preference are different kinds of information, and they should not be interchangeable just because both appear in prose. Attempts are auditable workflow records. Hindsight memories are retrieved context. The model gets both, with clear instructions about the action it must take.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would not describe this as a mathematical guarantee that a model can never repeat a failed fix. A model can misunderstand context or produce an unexpected response. The engineering goal is narrower and testable: preserve the outcomes, place failed attempts in front of the model, instruct it not to repeat them, and keep the proposed next action visible to support staff. If a hard prohibition is required for a particular class of operation, enforce that in application logic rather than trusting prompt wording.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Retrieve, reason, record
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For each reply, the backend saves the incoming customer message first. It then recalls Hindsight memories using a query formed from the ticket subject and current message. The recalled results and recent conversation are passed to the model. After generation, the backend separates customer-facing text from a metadata block, updates the ticket and attempt records, retains the exchange in Hindsight, and evaluates escalation policies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The memory call is kept out of the event loop’s blocking path. The service wraps the synchronous SDK call with &lt;code&gt;asyncio.to_thread&lt;/code&gt; and updates its status only after a successful call:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;to_thread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;except&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;MemoryNotConfigured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;except&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Exception&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;__name__&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;MemoryServiceError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_success_at&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;utcnow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That wrapper gives the API a consistent boundary around configuration and service failures. A missing or unavailable memory service should be observable as such; the application should not quietly pretend that recall happened. In a production deployment, I would pair this boundary with timeouts, retry policy appropriate to the request path, and operational alerts based on memory availability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The streaming path follows the same sequence while emitting status and response deltas over server-sent events. It holds back a short suffix of generated text so a metadata delimiter split across token chunks is not accidentally shown to the customer. Once the model’s metadata block begins, it accumulates that separately. The customer sees the reply as it arrives; the backend still gets structured fields to record the proposed solution, intent, category, and priority.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A concrete interaction
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine a customer whose card keeps failing during checkout. On the first ticket, the agent suggests removing and re-adding the card. The backend stores that proposal as a pending attempt. The customer replies that it did not work, and the next update marks the attempt failed. The exchange is also retained in that customer’s Hindsight bank.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Later, the customer opens a related ticket and says checkout still fails. The agent recalls relevant customer context, reads the new ticket’s attempt history, and gets the failed card re-add step in a dedicated prompt section. Its instructions tell it to propose a fresh alternative, acknowledge the failed step, and avoid claiming it has performed irreversible actions such as issuing a refund or resetting an account. The draft’s proposed fix is recorded as a new pending attempt, ready for an agent or customer outcome to resolve.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This combination is more useful than relying on memory alone. The ticket’s attempt rows provide precise, inspectable outcomes for that issue. Hindsight can surface relevant context across tickets without requiring the application to copy and query every old conversation itself. The model receives a compact working context; the application retains the durable operational facts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If attempts continue to fail, escalation rules can create an internal review record. The policy engine can also flag repeated complaints, unresolved tickets past a configured age, and high-priority issues. The escalation snapshot includes the ticket history, attempts, customer information, and related tickets so a human can pick up the case with context. In a complete deployment, those policies and routing integrations should be backed by operational monitoring and clear ownership; creating a record is only the first step in a reliable handoff.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Separate memory from workflow state
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A semantic memory store is useful for retrieving context, but it should not become the only place that records whether a fix failed. Outcomes need explicit fields, audit history, and predictable updates. Use the memory layer to help find context; use the relational database for decisions the workflow must enforce and explain.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Persist outcomes, not just transcripts
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A long conversation is not a reliable representation of what the support process tried. Explicit resolution attempts make the failure legible to both the next model call and a human agent. If the outcome is unknown, represent it as unknown or pending rather than inferring success from silence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Make memory failures visible
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A system that silently substitutes “no memories” when recall fails is difficult to debug and can produce misleading confidence. Expose whether recall and retain succeeded, track the last successful call and last error, and design the product’s fallback behavior intentionally. Memory is a dependency with failure modes, not a prompt decoration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Keep model output inside application boundaries
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The model can suggest a category, priority, and solution, but the backend validates categories and only allows priority to rise. It records the proposal as pending instead of treating generated text as completed work. That separation is essential whenever a reply can affect customer expectations or downstream operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  5. Use memory to reduce repetition, then verify the result
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recall can help an agent avoid asking the customer to start over. It cannot prove a fix worked. The system still needs a follow-up outcome, whether from the customer or a human agent, before a suggestion becomes a successful resolution. That feedback is what makes the next interaction better grounded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The useful promise of this design is not that a language model will never make a mistake. It is that the support system can remember what it tried, carry the outcome forward, and make the next response answerable to that history. Hindsight supplies the cross-ticket context; explicit attempt records keep the workflow honest. That is the foundation I would want before trusting an AI agent with a customer who has already heard “try it again.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rendering a page should not change anything. &lt;a href="https://nakodo.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Nakodo&lt;/a&gt; breaks that rule in five places, and every one of them is on purpose, so I went and wrote down the rule they actually follow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The app runs outreach campaigns for brands: it finds creators or local businesses that fit a brief, writes to them, and hands over the ones that say yes, which is the bit described on &lt;a href="https://nakodo.app/how-it-works" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;how it works&lt;/a&gt;. Every page in this post is behind the login, which turns out to be half the reason the pattern is safe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  One: the first page you load creates your account row
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;requireUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SessionUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/login&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getProfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;insert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;profiles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onConflictDoNothing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Sign-up creates a profile row. Accounts created any other way, by an operator or at the command line or by a provider that let somebody in through a path we did not build, do not have one, and the first page they load makes it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cost on the ordinary path is zero extra queries, because &lt;code&gt;getProfile&lt;/code&gt; is what the app's layout reads anyway and both functions are wrapped in React's &lt;code&gt;cache&lt;/code&gt;, so the whole thing is one lookup per request however many components ask. The insert is &lt;code&gt;onConflictDoNothing&lt;/code&gt;, so two parallel requests from the same new account produce one row and no error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Two: your billing period rolls forward the first time it is read
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentPeriodStart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;addMonths&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscriptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;currentPeriodStart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;currentPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscriptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;returning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Usage limits count from &lt;code&gt;currentPeriodStart&lt;/code&gt;, and on a free plan there is no Stripe webhook to move it. So the period moves when somebody reads it, in a &lt;code&gt;while&lt;/code&gt; loop rather than a single addition, because an account that comes back after four months needs the current window and not the next one after the one it missed. That mechanism has its own post, including what it does about a signup on the 31st.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What matters here is the shape, which is the same as the first one: a predicate that is false in the steady state, and a write that only happens on the edge.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Three: a cut-off research run is put right by the next person who looks at the list
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Research runs inside the request that started it, up to about two minutes of crawling and model calls. If that request dies, the campaign row is left saying &lt;code&gt;researching&lt;/code&gt; and nothing in the system is watching it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Research cut off mid-run is put right only when the list shows some, so&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the page doesn't write on every visit.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;some&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;researchIsStale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;recoverStaleResearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;campaignsNow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;researchIsStale&lt;/code&gt; is a pure function over rows the page has already loaded: status &lt;code&gt;researching&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;updatedAt&lt;/code&gt; more than three minutes ago. Only if one row in the list matches does the write happen at all, and the write is a single statement whose &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; repeats the same conditions, scoped to the signed-in user:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sql&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`case when &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;brief&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is null then 'failed'
                   when &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;launchedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is not null then 'paused'
                   else 'draft' end`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;pauseMode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sql&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`case when &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;brief&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is not null and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;launchedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is not null then 'both' end`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;pauseReason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;researching&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;lt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;updatedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;STALE_RESEARCH_MS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;returning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Three &lt;code&gt;CASE&lt;/code&gt; expressions instead of three round trips, because where the campaign should land depends on what it already had: a campaign with no brief failed, a campaign that was live comes back paused with everything stopped for a person to resume deliberately, and anything else is a draft. Then each recovered campaign refunds the research run it never finished, so a crash does not cost somebody a unit of their plan.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The honest part: &lt;strong&gt;this repair only runs if somebody looks.&lt;/strong&gt; There is no cron sweeping for stale research. An account that starts a campaign, closes the tab at the wrong second and never comes back has a campaign that says &lt;code&gt;researching&lt;/code&gt; until the day it loads a page. For a state that only exists because a request died, and that is only visible on the page that fixes it, I think that is the right trade, and I would not have believed it was deliberate if I had found it without the comment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Four: a page read fetches a logo from somebody else's website, after it has answered
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This one looks worst and I like it most.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;after&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fillLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;after&lt;/code&gt; is Next's post-response hook: the callback runs once the response has been flushed, so the reader waits for none of it. Inside:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fillLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{...}[])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;logoUrl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;researching&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;has&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;logo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;findSiteLogo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;domain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;logoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;logo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;isNull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;logoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)));&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Campaigns created before the app kept logos have &lt;code&gt;logoUrl&lt;/code&gt; of &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;, which means "never looked". The first page that would display one goes and looks, which is the only honest way to backfill a column whose value lives on another company's website and that nobody should have to wait for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Four guards, and each one is answering a different "what if":&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;logoUrl === null&lt;/code&gt; is the predicate. The steady state writes nothing, and &lt;code&gt;""&lt;/code&gt; is the marker for "we looked and found nothing", so a brand with no usable icon is asked about once, ever.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;.slice(0, 5)&lt;/code&gt; bounds the work. A list of twenty campaigns does not fire twenty outbound requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The module-level &lt;code&gt;Set&lt;/code&gt; stops the same render pass and two quick page loads on one instance from doing the same lookup twice. It is per instance, so on a serverless platform it is a hint and not a lock.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; carries &lt;code&gt;isNull(campaigns.logoUrl)&lt;/code&gt; as well, which is the actual lock: whichever instance writes first wins, and the second update touches no rows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The thing I had not thought about until writing this down: the app-router prefetches on hover, so moving your mouse over a campaign link can run the layout, and the layout is the second &lt;code&gt;fillLogos&lt;/code&gt; call site. A prefetch can start a logo lookup. Because the work is idempotent, bounded and once-per-campaign, that is harmless, and if any of those three stopped being true it would be a bug that only ever happened to people who move their mouse.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Five: opening a support thread is what marks it read
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lines&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;linesOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Reading it is what clears the mark. Done after the lines are in hand, so a&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// failure here leaves the mark rather than hiding an unread reply.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;markRead&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;supportTickets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;readAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;supportTickets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;getThread&lt;/code&gt; has exactly two callers, the page that shows a thread and the action that replies to it, and both pass &lt;code&gt;{ markRead: true }&lt;/code&gt;. The option exists anyway, because the admin panel counts tickets rather than opening them today, and the day an operator view does open one, the mark-read has to be a thing it can decline: an operator reading your ticket must not clear your unread dot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ordering comment is the whole decision. Load the messages first, then clear the mark, so if the query that clears it fails the user sees the messages &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; keeps the unread dot. The other order loses a reply quietly, and the unread state in this app is &lt;code&gt;read_at is null or last_message_at &amp;gt; read_at&lt;/code&gt;, which means "read" is a claim about an instant rather than a boolean, and a wrong claim is permanent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The rule all five follow
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reading them together, there are four properties, and I would now refuse a sixth one that broke any of them:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A predicate that is false on the ordinary visit.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;!profile&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;periodEnd &amp;lt;= now&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;some(isStale)&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;logoUrl === null&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;unread&lt;/code&gt;. If a page writes on every read, it is not a repair, it is an unlogged mutation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Idempotent, and safe when two requests race.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;onConflictDoNothing&lt;/code&gt; on one, the same conditions repeated in the &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; on the other three, a single statement for the fourth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Scoped to the reader.&lt;/strong&gt; Every one of these &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; clauses carries the signed-in user's id, so the worst a read can do is repair its own account's rows. None of these paths is reachable without a session: the auth boundary is one allowlist and none of these pages are on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Anything slow goes after the response.&lt;/strong&gt; The only one that touches the network is the only one wrapped in &lt;code&gt;after&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And one property they all lack, which I am leaving alone: none of them writes an audit row. The audit log is for things a person or an operator did, and "the system noticed something was stale" is not one of those. The repair is visible in the row it fixed, and if I needed a trail of repairs I would want it in the run log, not in the log that answers "who changed my account".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Five reads that write, in 72,683 lines. The reason to count them is that each one was obviously correct on the day I wrote it, and the fifth one is only obviously correct because of a comment about the order of two queries.&lt;/p&gt;
